   "subject": "Re: Sparse matrix issue with RTMB",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><br></div><div>1.</div><div>The error you get is when converting from AD dense matrix to AD sparse matrix. I.e</div><div><br></div><div>as(matrix(advector(c(1,0,0,0)),2), &quot;sparseMatrix&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>which was not available in RTMB until recently in the development version.</div><div><br></div><div>2.</div><div>A worked out example on how to use dgmrf is available here:</div><div><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/RTMB/blob/master/RTMB/inst/tinytest/test-model-spde.R\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/RTMB/blob/master/RTMB/inst/tinytest/test-model-spde.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461612164000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RbDnfn9dlYNP3_Uueb0mm\">https://github.com/kaskr/RTMB/blob/master/RTMB/inst/tinytest/test-model-spde.R</a><br></span></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
